counterfactuals.output:
An ablation applicator for ablating tissue of a blood vessel, comprising:

a tubular body configured for insertion into the blood vessel and having a distal treatment region;

an ablation medium supply line extending through the tubular body and configured to deliver an ablation medium to the distal treatment region;

a plurality of spaced apertures formed in the distal treatment region and in fluid communication with the ablation medium supply line, the spaced apertures being configured to discharge the ablation medium at spaced locations along the blood vessel tissue;

a control mechanism operably coupled to the ablation medium supply line and configured to regulate delivery of the ablation medium through the spaced apertures;

at least one temperature sensor disposed at or near the distal treatment region and configured to sense temperature associated with the blood vessel tissue during ablation; and

a return line extending through the tubular body and configured to remove at least a portion of the ablation medium from the distal treatment region, wherein the return line comprises a thermally resistant and biocompatible material suitable for exposure to the ablation medium.
